    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Riders With A Passenger Parking Strategy</h1>
    <p>Parking is the least glamorous part of a motorbike rental and the part where most avoidable losses happen, because a bike is never more anonymous than when it sits among two hundred identical ones. For a pair, parking is also a logistics problem: two helmets, two sets of belongings and a machine that carries double the value of a solo setup. A strategy means the bike's location is a decision, not an accident, and that decision gets made before the destination, not after three laps of the block.</p>
    <p>This page is the parking chapter of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster for riders carrying a passenger. Verified rental prices and periods are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, general questions are collected on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the machine you will be parking was chosen using the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/riders-with-a-passenger-bike-choice/">bike-choice page for two-up riders</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">How Hanoi parking actually works</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The three questions to ask at any destination</a></li>
